---
// The Maester Manifesto, laid out like the one on maester.cloud (website/src/app/pages/manifesto.astro in the
// maester-cloud repository): a hero, the text with its key lines pulled out as highlights, and a closing card.
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
	title="The Maester Manifesto"
	description="Why Maester exists, why its core will remain open source, and how the community can make security testing available to everyone."
>
	<section class="hero">
		<div class="wrap">
			<span class="kicker">The Maester Manifesto</span>
			<h1>Make security testing open, reusable, and available to everyone.</h1>
			<p class="lede">Maester exists to turn security guidance into tests that anyone can run, understand, and improve.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<article class="body">
		<div class="wrap">
			<div class="prose">
				<p>Maester exists to make cloud security testing open, reusable, and available to everyone.</p>
				<p>
					The core idea is simple: security guidance should not only be written down. It should be executable. If a setting
					matters, if a risky default is buried ten pages deep in a portal, or if a standard says something should be
					configured a certain way, people should be able to run a test, see the result, understand the rationale, and
					improve.
				</p>
				<p>
					This should not require a large budget, a specialist team, or access to expensive tooling. Individual admins, small
					security teams, nonprofits, schools, startups, and organizations in developing nations deserve useful security
					checks, too.
				</p>
			</div>

			<aside class="why">
				<span class="label">Why it matters</span>
				<div class="why__text">
					<p>
						That part is personal to me. I grew up in Sri Lanka. I know what it means when useful technology exists, but is
						priced out of reach for the people and organizations that could benefit from it most.
					</p>
					<p class="strong">
						Security should not become another place where the gap between well-funded organizations and everyone else gets
						wider.
					</p>
					<p class="close">Maester exists to help close that gap.</p>
				</div>
			</aside>

			<section class="part">
				<span class="kicker">Open Source Core</span>
				<h2>Maester is open source and will remain open source.</h2>
				<div class="free">
					<span class="label label--ember">Free, and staying free</span>
					<div class="free__lines">
						<p>The core framework will remain <span class="ember">free</span>.</p>
						<p>The included core tests will remain <span class="ember">free</span>.</p>
						<p>Running Maester locally in your own environment will remain <span class="ember">free</span>.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="prose">
					<p>
						Anyone should be able to take Maester, install it, inspect it, adapt it, run it, and use it in their own
						workflows. That includes individual admins, internal security teams, consultants, MSPs, vendors, auditors,
						educators, and community contributors.
					</p>
					<p>
						An objective of the Maester project is to minimize duplication of effort, provide a reference model across
						environments, and allow for that to be reused within the authority provided by the MIT license.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="part">
				<span class="kicker">A Community Project</span>
				<h2>Community-driven, not a company-owned control point.</h2>
				<div class="prose">
					<p>
						Commercial organizations should be able to build services around Maester without needing permission from one
						vendor. The healthiest version of Maester is one where many people and organizations contribute to the open core,
						build on it, and help improve it.
					</p>
					<p>
						Jozra is Merill's company, and it will be one of the commercial participants building around Maester. I (Merill)
						will continue investing heavily in the open project while also building hosted services that make Maester easier
						to run and use, providing paid support, and offering commercial licensing for organizations that cannot use open
						source software. The open framework itself should stand on its own as a community asset.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="cards">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>For individuals and small teams</h3>
					<p>Maester should be something you can use without asking for budget.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>For organizations building on Maester</h3>
					<p>Help fund the initiative through sponsorship, contribution, or commercial support.</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="supporters">
				<span class="label label--ember">Supporters</span>
				<h2>Help us build it, in the open.</h2>
				<p>
					Maester is built by volunteers and by the people and organizations who sponsor them. Sponsorship pays for maintainer
					time and the test tenants every check is proven against, and keeps the core framework and tests open, current, and
					free for everyone: the admins, nonprofits, schools, and small teams who could never buy this otherwise.
				</p>
				<p>
					Using Maester at work? Ask your organization to <b>sponsor</b> the project, or run it with{' '}
					<b>Maester Cloud</b>: every subscription helps fund the open core.
				</p>
				<div class="actions">
					<a href="/sponsor" class="btn btn--primary">Sponsor Maester</a>
					<a href="https://maester.cloud" class="btn btn--ghost">Maester Cloud ↗</a>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="mission">
				<span class="label label--soft">The mission is simple</span>
				<p>Make security testing open, reusable, and available to everyone.</p>
				<div class="actions">
					<a href="/sponsor" class="btn btn--ghost">Support the mission</a>
				</div>
			</section>
		</div>
	</article>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
	.wrap {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 56rem;
		margin-inline: auto;
		padding-inline: 1.5rem;
	}
	.kicker,
	.label {
		font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.12em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
	}
	.label {
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}
	/* maester.cloud's red: #d22c31 in light, the lighter ember in dark. */
	.label--ember,
	.ember {
		color: var(--mt-ember);
	}

	/* Hero */
	.hero {
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--mt-line);
		background: var(--sl-color-black);
		padding-block: 4rem;
	}
	h1 {
		margin: 1rem 0 0;
		max-width: 48rem;
		font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 6vw, 3.75rem);
		font-weight: 700;
		line-height: 1.1;
		letter-spacing: -0.025em;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}
	.lede {
		margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
		max-width: 42rem;
		font-size: 1.125rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}

	/* Body */
	.body {
		background: var(--mt-canvas);
		padding-block: 4rem;
	}
	.prose {
		max-width: 48rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1.5rem;
		font-size: 1.02rem;
		line-height: 2;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}
	.prose p,
	.why__text p,
	.free__lines p,
	.supporters p,
	.mission p,
	.card p {
		margin: 0;
	}

	/* Why it matters */
	.why {
		margin-block: 3rem;
		max-width: 48rem;
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
		border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--sl-color-white) 20%, transparent);
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--sl-color-gray-6) 45%, transparent);
		padding: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
	}
	.why__text {
		margin-top: 1rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1.25rem;
		font-size: 1.125rem;
		line-height: 2;
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}
	.why__text .strong {
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.why__text .close {
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
	}

	/* Sections */
	.part {
		max-width: 48rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--mt-line);
		padding-top: 3rem;
		margin-top: 3.5rem;
	}
	.part:first-of-type {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	h2 {
		margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
		font-size: 1.875rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: -0.025em;
		line-height: 1.2;
	}
	.part .prose {
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}

	/* Free, and staying free */
	.free {
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
		border: 1px solid rgba(210, 44, 49, 0.2);
		background: rgba(210, 44, 49, 0.04);
		padding: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.25rem);
	}
	.free__lines {
		margin-top: 1rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.625rem;
		font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.6vw, 1.5rem);
		font-weight: 700;
		line-height: 1.35;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}

	/* Two cards */
	.cards {
		margin-top: 3.5rem;
		max-width: 48rem;
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
	}
	.card {
		border-radius: 1rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--mt-line);
		background: var(--sl-color-black);
		padding: 1.5rem;
	}
	.card h3 {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 1rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
	}
	.card p {
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		line-height: 1.5rem;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}

	/* Supporters */
	.supporters {
		margin-top: 3.5rem;
		max-width: 48rem;
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
		border: 1px solid rgba(210, 44, 49, 0.2);
		background: rgba(210, 44, 49, 0.04);
		padding: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
	}
	.supporters h2 {
		font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 1.875rem);
	}
	.supporters p {
		margin-top: 1rem;
		font-size: 1.02rem;
		line-height: 2;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}
	.supporters p + p {
		margin-top: 0.75rem;
	}
	.supporters b {
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}

	/* Mission */
	.mission {
		margin-top: 2rem;
		max-width: 48rem;
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
		background: #18181b;
		border: 1px solid #27272a;
		color: #fff;
		padding: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3rem) clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
	}
	.label--soft {
		color: rgba(244, 244, 245, 0.8);
	}
	.mission p {
		margin-top: 1rem;
		font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.25rem);
		font-weight: 700;
		line-height: 1.2;
		letter-spacing: -0.025em;
	}

	/* Buttons */
	.actions {
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}
	.mission .actions {
		margin-top: 1.75rem;
	}
	.btn {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		min-height: 2.5rem;
		padding: 0.7rem 1.05rem;
		border-radius: 0.625rem;
		border: 1px solid transparent;
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		line-height: 1.15;
		text-decoration: none;
		transition: background-color 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;
	}
	.btn--primary {
		background: var(--sl-color-white);
		color: var(--sl-color-black);
	}
	.btn--primary:hover {
		opacity: 0.9;
	}
	.btn--ghost {
		background: var(--sl-color-black);
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
		border-color: var(--mt-line);
	}
	.btn--ghost:hover {
		border-color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
	}
	.mission .btn--ghost {
		background: #fff;
		color: #18181b;
		border-color: #fff;
	}

	@media (min-width: 40rem) {
		.hero,
		.body {
			padding-block: 6rem;
		}
	}
</style>
